From 71ecf2764098c61c2e9524ddce52df864ce957dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gregory Price <gourry@gourry.net>
Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 18:10:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Documentation/dax: document adistance attribute

Document the dax/kmem "adistance" sysfs knob:

  a read/write abstract distance that adjusts the placement of the
  private node node in the memory-tier hierarchy.

  retunable while the device is unplugged, and reset to the probe-time
  default whenever "private" is toggled.

Signed-off-by: Gregory Price <gourry@gourry.net>
---
 Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-bus-dax | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-bus-dax b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-bus-dax
index 6f2d5fc17e4..3735fce5846 100644
--- a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-bus-dax
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-bus-dax
@@ -211,6 +211,21 @@ Description:
 		compact/reclaim risks failing higher-order (THP) allocations for
 		want of a given order; with reclaim, THP is allowed.
 
+What:		/sys/bus/dax/devices/daxX.Y/adistance
+Date:		June, 2026
+KernelVersion:	v6.21
+Contact:	nvdimm@lists.linux.dev
+Description:
+		(RW) dax_kmem "private" mode only (hidden otherwise).
+
+		Abstract distance that adjusts the placement of the private node
+		in the memory-tier hierarchy (larger is a lower tier).
+
+		May only be written while the device is "unplugged".
+		Toggling "private" resets it to the probe-time default.
+
+		No effect if CAP_DEMOTION is not also selected.
+
 What:		/sys/bus/dax/devices/daxX.Y/reclaim
 What:		/sys/bus/dax/devices/daxX.Y/user_numa
 What:		/sys/bus/dax/devices/daxX.Y/hotunplug
-- 
2.55.0

